    "_doc": "The gore rework (docs/gore/gore_rework_2026-11.md), read by GoreFx (gravelight/world/vfx/gore_fx.gd). Only the Gore setting 'full' bleeds. budget: the hard cap of marks per kind on the world (all of them instances of one MultiMesh; a full kind reuses its oldest), scaled by quality.<level>.gore and by web_scale on the Compatibility renderer. per_frame: at most this many raycasts and new marks in one physics frame. horde: with more than 'from' live zombies the chances and particle counts below fall linearly to 'min' at 'to' zombies; zombies leave boot prints only while at most zombie_prints_max are alive. classes.<weapon class>: mist / drops / chunks = particles per hit (the mist leaves the entry, the drops and the meat the far side); exit = chance that a hit marks what is behind the body within reach metres, size [far, near] metres; floor = chance of drops on the floor under it; drip = chance that a wall spatter runs; screen = blood on the lens when it happens within screen.near_m of the camera (0..1 of a full spatter). 'default' is everything that is not a bullet (the knife, a sever, a bot's report without a weapon). wet_color / dry_color: sRGB, dark on purpose; it dries over dry_seconds. pool_size: metres across, pool_grow_seconds: how long it spreads. spurt: the neck after a head came off (slots at once, seconds). tracks: who treads in a pool younger than wet_seconds leaves print_steps boot prints; a crawler drags a smear for smear_steps marks; pools are checked every scan_seconds. screen: the lens spatter (fade_seconds, on_hurt = the amount when the player is hit, clear_radius = the middle of the view that always stays clean, 1 = the screen's half height). hands: blood on the first-person hands and sleeves (the arms shader's gl_hand_blood): each lens spatter adds per_spatter times its amount, and it wears off over seconds. death_spatters: cast-off marks laid around a body with its pool.",
